Security and Risk Management

This domain focuses on defining security goals, mitigating risks, ensuring compliance with regulations, and establishing business continuity plans.
It involves reducing risks to critical assets and data, adhering to internal policies and external regulations, and preparing for disaster recovery.
Asset Security

This domain is concerned with securing both digital and physical assets, including the proper handling of data throughout its lifecycle.
It emphasizes protecting sensitive information like PII (Personally Identifiable Information) and ensuring secure storage, maintenance, retention, and destruction of data.
Security Architecture and Engineering

This domain aims to optimize data security by implementing effective tools, systems, and processes.
A core concept is shared responsibility, where all individuals within an organization contribute to lowering risk and maintaining security.
Communication and Network Security

This domain focuses on managing and securing physical networks and wireless communications.
It involves protecting an organization's data and communications, especially for remote workers, by preventing vulnerabilities from insecure connections like public Wi-Fi or Bluetooth.
